 "raw_output": "Amazon's total revenue rose about 31.0% from fiscal Q1 2024 to fiscal Q4 2024.\n\nThe excerpts don't report Q4 2024 revenue directly, so I derived it from the full-year and nine-month figures:\n\n- Q4 2024 net sales = FY2024 total net sales \u2212 nine-month 2024 net sales = $637,959M \u2212 $450,167M = $187,792M.\n- Q1 2024 net sales (from the Q1 2025 10-Q comparative column) = $143,313M.\n- Percent change = (187,792 \u2212 143,313) / 143,313 = 44,479 / 143,313 \u2248 31.04%.\n\n{\"value\": 31.04, \"unit\": \"percent\", \"choice\": null, \"status\": \"answered\"}",
